WEBVTT

00:00:00.015 --> 00:00:06.102
When several source columns become one value column, PostgreSQL needs a common data type.

00:00:06.102 --> 00:00:12.387
If one metric is integer and another is numeric, explicit casts may be helpful.

00:00:12.387 --> 00:00:16.947
The patient metric example casts selected values to numeric.

00:00:16.947 --> 00:00:21.407
Do not let type coercion become an accidental part of the reshape.

00:00:21.407 --> 00:00:24.692
Choose the long value type deliberately.

00:00:24.692 --> 00:00:31.187
Connect this idea to a BI dashboard turning monthly categories into presentation columns.

00:00:31.187 --> 00:00:36.987
Ask what could go wrong if the concept were misunderstood: could rows be duplicated,

00:00:36.987 --> 00:00:45.087
important records disappear, categories be interpreted incorrectly, or a report become difficult to reproduce?

00:00:45.087 --> 00:00:51.132
A strong analyst can explain both the SQL operation and the assumption behind it.

00:00:51.132 --> 00:00:56.880
After the example, summarize the idea in one plain-language sentence before moving on.
